IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-ch3-offers.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 3 -- "Squeeze-out" and "Sell-out":
-- takeover offers (ss 974 to 978), joint offers (s 987) and interpretation (ss 988 to 991).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- Seams (PLAN.md section 4): s 1159 (subsidiary, the keel), s 823 (voting power, coa18), s 1173(1) (regulated market, the keel).
-- Convention (rulings of 2026-11-05): a "where" or "if" that fails answers JUST FALSE, and a definition by "means" answers JUST FALSE
-- outside it; a list with no "only" or "means" answers NOTHING outside it. Marginal readings are listed in NOTES.md.

§ `Part 28, Chapter 3: "Squeeze-out" and "Sell-out"`

§§ `Interpretation (ss 988 to 991)`

-- s 991(1): "the company" means the company whose shares are the subject of a takeover offer.
-- src:13857 | “the company” means the company whose shares are the subject of a takeover offer;
@ref s 991(1)“the company” Interpretation (src:13857-13857)
GIVEN `the company's shares are the subject of a takeover offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(1) the company is the company for the purposes of Chapter 3` MEANS
    IF `the company's shares are the subject of a takeover offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the company” means the company whose shares are the subject of a takeover offer"

-- s 991(1): "date of the offer" means the date of publication where the offer is published, otherwise (or where notices are given before publication) the date when the first notices are given.
-- src:13858 | “date of the offer” means—
@ref s 991(1)“date of the offer” Interpretation (src:13858-13858)
GIVEN `the offer is published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of publication` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `notices of the offer were given before the date of publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date when notices of the offer (or the first such notices) are given` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 991(1) the date of the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is published` AND NOT (`notices of the offer were given before the date of publication`)
    THEN `the date of publication`
    ELSE `the date when notices of the offer (or the first such notices) are given`

-- s 991(1): "non-voting shares" means shares that are not voting shares; "voting rights" and "voting shares" as in section 971(1) but for the company of the Chapter.
-- src:13862 | “non-voting shares” means shares that are not voting shares;
@ref s 991(1)“non-voting shares” Interpretation (src:13862-13862)
GIVEN `s 991(1) the shares are voting shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(1) the shares are non-voting shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 991(1) the shares are voting shares`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non-voting shares” means shares that are not voting shares"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the shares are voting shares is not known

-- src:13864 | “voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances;
@ref s 991(1)“voting rights” Interpretation (src:13864-13864)
GIVEN `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(1) the rights are voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including rights that arise only in certain circumstances
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances"

-- src:13865 | “voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights.
@ref s 991(1)“voting shares” Interpretation (src:13865-13865)
GIVEN `the shares carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(1) the shares are voting shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares carry voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights"

-- s 991(1): "offeror" means (subject to section 987) the person making a takeover offer.
-- src:13863 | “offeror” means (subject to section 987) the person making a takeover offer;
@ref s 991(1)“offeror” Interpretation (src:13863-13863)
GIVEN `the person is making the takeover offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(1) the person is the offeror` MEANS
    IF `the person is making the takeover offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (for a joint offer, section 987(7) reads the offeror as the joint offerors or any of them)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offeror” means (subject to section 987) the person making a takeover offer"

-- s 991(2): a person contracts unconditionally to acquire shares if his entitlement is not (or no longer) subject to conditions or all conditions have been met.
-- src:13866 | (2) For the purposes of this Chapter a person contracts unconditionally to acquire shares if his entitlement under the contract to acquire them is not (or is no longer) subject to conditions or if all conditions to which it was subject have been met.
-- src:13867 | A reference to a contract becoming unconditional is to be read accordingly.
@ref s 991(2) Interpretation (src:13866-13867)
GIVEN `the entitlement under the contract is not (or is no longer) subject to conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the conditions to which the entitlement was subject have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 991(2) the person contracts unconditionally to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement under the contract is not (or is no longer) subject to conditions` OR `all the conditions to which the entitlement was subject have been met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person contracts unconditionally to acquire shares if his entitlement under the contract to acquire them is not (or is no longer) subject to conditions or if all conditions to which it was subject have been met"

-- s 989(1): securities convertible into, or entitling the holder to subscribe for, shares are treated as shares for the Chapter.
-- src:13844 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter securities of a company are treated as shares in the company if they are convertible into or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares.
-- src:13845 | References to the holder of shares or a shareholder are to be read accordingly.
@ref s 989(1) Convertible securities (src:13844-13845)
GIVEN `the securities are convertible into shares in the company or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 989(1) the securities are treated as shares in the company` MEANS
    IF `the securities are convertible into shares in the company or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "securities of a company are treated as shares in the company if they are convertible into or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares"

-- s 989(2): subsection (1) is not to be read as requiring such securities to be treated as shares of the same class as the shares they convert into, or as other securities of the same underlying class.
-- src:13846 | (2) Subsection (1) is not to be read as requiring any securities to be treated—
-- src:13847 | (a) as shares of the same class as those into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe, or
-- src:13848 | (b) as shares of the same class as other securities by reason only that the shares into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe are of the same class.
@ref s 989(2) Convertible securities (src:13846-13848)
GIVEN `the securities are to be treated as shares of the same class as those into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities are to be treated as shares of the same class as other securities by reason only that the underlying shares are of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 989(2) subsection (1) requires the securities to be treated as shares of the same class` MEANS
    IF `the securities are to be treated as shares of the same class as those into which they are convertible or for which the holder is entitled to subscribe` OR `the securities are to be treated as shares of the same class as other securities by reason only that the underlying shares are of the same class`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) is not to be read as requiring any securities to be treated"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what subsection (1) does not require, not what it does

-- s 990(2): the subsection applies to a company with voting shares, or debentures carrying voting rights, admitted to trading on a regulated market.
-- src:13851 | (2) This subsection applies to a company that has voting shares, or debentures carrying voting rights, which are admitted to trading on a regulated market.
@ref s 990(2) Debentures carrying voting rights (src:13851-13851)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the voting shares or debentures carrying voting rights are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 990(2) the company is one to which the subsection applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the voting shares or debentures carrying voting rights are admitted to trading on a regulated market`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection "applies to a company that has voting shares, or debentures carrying voting rights, which are admitted to trading on a regulated market"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "regulated market" is Article 2.1.13 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 (section 1173(1))

-- s 990(1): debentures issued by such a company are treated as shares in the company if they carry voting rights.
-- src:13850 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter debentures issued by a company to which subsection (2) applies are treated as shares in the company if they carry voting rights.
@ref s 990(1) Debentures carrying voting rights (src:13850-13850)
GIVEN `s 990(2) the company is one to which the subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the debentures carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 990(1) the debentures are treated as shares in the company` MEANS
    IF `s 990(2) the company is one to which the subsection applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the debentures carry voting rights`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "debentures issued by a company to which subsection (2) applies are treated as shares in the company if they carry voting rights"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for "debentures issued by a company to which subsection (2) applies"

-- s 990(3): in relation to debentures treated as shares, references to the holder or shareholder are read accordingly, and references to shares being allotted as debentures being issued.
DECLARE `s 990(3) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 990(3)(a) a reference to the holder of shares or a shareholder`
    `s 990(3)(b) a reference to shares being allotted`
    `s 990(3) another reference`

-- src:13852 | (3) In this Chapter, in relation to debentures treated as shares by virtue of subsection (1)—
-- src:13853 | (a) references to the holder of shares or a shareholder are to be read accordingly;
-- src:13854 | (b) references to shares being allotted are to be read as references to debentures being issued.
@ref s 990(3) Debentures carrying voting rights (src:13852-13854)
GIVEN `s 990(1) the debentures are treated as shares in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      reference IS A `s 990(3) reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 990(3) the reference is read in relation to the debentures` MEANS
    IF `s 990(1) the debentures are treated as shares in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER reference
         WHEN `s 990(3)(a) a reference to the holder of shares or a shareholder` THEN JUST TRUE -- read as a reference to the holder of the debentures
         WHEN `s 990(3)(b) a reference to shares being allotted` THEN JUST TRUE -- read as a reference to debentures being issued
         WHEN `s 990(3) another reference` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): only the two references are read accordingly
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is "in relation to debentures treated as shares by virtue of subsection (1)"

-- s 988(2): a company is a fellow subsidiary of another body corporate if both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate but neither is a subsidiary of the other.
-- src:13825 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) a company is a fellow subsidiary of another body corporate if both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate but neither is a subsidiary of the other.
@ref s 988(2) Associates (src:13825-13825)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) one is a subsidiary of the other` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(2) the company is a fellow subsidiary of the other body corporate` MEANS
    IF `s 1159(1) both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 1159(1) one is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is a fellow subsidiary of another body corporate if both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate but neither is a subsidiary of the other"
    ELSE IF `s 1159(1) both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1159(1) one is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether either is a subsidiary of the other is section 1159(1)'s answer

-- s 988(3): the offeror has a substantial interest in a body corporate if the body or its directors are accustomed to act on his directions, or he is entitled to exercise or control one-third or more of the voting power at its general meetings.
-- src:13826 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(c) an offeror has a substantial interest in a body corporate if—
-- src:13827 | (a) the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or
-- src:13828 | (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of the body.
-- src:13829 | Subsections (2) and (3) of section 823 (which contain provision about when a person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power) apply for the purposes of this subsection as they apply for the purposes of that section.
@ref s 988(3) Associates (src:13826-13829)
GIVEN `the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the offeror's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 823(2)-(3) the voting power at general meetings of the body that the offeror is treated as entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting power at general meetings of the body` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(3) the offeror has a substantial interest in the body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the offeror's directions or instructions` OR (`the total voting power at general meetings of the body` GREATER THAN 0 AND `s 823(2)-(3) the voting power at general meetings of the body that the offeror is treated as entitled to exercise or control` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `the total voting power at general meetings of the body`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offeror has a substantial interest in a body corporate if— (a) the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of the body"

-- s 988(5): an agreement is an excluded agreement (a) if it is not legally binding, unless it involves mutuality, or (b) if it is an underwriting agreement confined to that purpose.
-- src:13834 | (5) An agreement is an “excluded agreement”—
-- src:13835 | (a) if it is not legally binding, unless it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it, or
-- src:13836 | (b) if it is an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company, provided the agreement is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it.
@ref s 988(5) Associates (src:13834-13836)
GIVEN `the agreement is not legally binding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(5) the agreement is an excluded agreement` MEANS
    IF (`the agreement is not legally binding` AND NOT (`it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it`)) OR (`it is an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company` AND `it is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An agreement is an “excluded agreement”— (a) if it is not legally binding, unless it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it, or (b) if it is an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company"

-- s 988(4): an agreement is a share acquisition agreement if it is (a) for the acquisition of shares to which the offer relates, (b) imposes obligations or restrictions on use, retention or disposal, and (c) is not an excluded agreement.
-- src:13830 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1)(d) an agreement is a share acquisition agreement if—
-- src:13831 | (a) it is an agreement for the acquisition of, or of an interest in, shares to which the offer relates,
-- src:13832 | (b) it includes provisions imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties to it with respect to their use, retention or disposal of such shares, or their interests in such shares, acquired in pursuance of the agreement (whether or not together with any other shares to which the offer relates or any other interests of theirs in such shares), and
-- src:13833 | (c) it is not an excluded agreement (see subsection (5)).
@ref s 988(4) Associates (src:13830-13833)
GIVEN `it is an agreement for the acquisition of, or of an interest in, shares to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes provisions imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties with respect to their use, retention or disposal of such shares, or their interests in such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988(5) the agreement is an excluded agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(4) the agreement is a share acquisition agreement` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it is an agreement for the acquisition of, or of an interest in, shares to which the offer relates`)) OR (NOT (`it includes provisions imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties with respect to their use, retention or disposal of such shares, or their interests in such shares`)) OR (`s 988(5) the agreement is an excluded agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an agreement is a share acquisition agreement if— (a) it is an agreement for the acquisition of, or of an interest in, shares to which the offer relates"
    ELSE IF `s 988(5) the agreement is an excluded agreement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the agreement is an excluded agreement is not known

-- s 988(6): the use of interests in shares is the exercise of any rights, or of any control or influence, arising from them.
-- src:13837 | (6) The reference in subsection (4)(b) to the use of interests in shares is to the exercise of any rights or of any control or influence arising from those interests (including the right to enter into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person).
@ref s 988(6) Associates (src:13837-13837)
GIVEN `the thing is the exercise of any rights, or of any control or influence, arising from the interests (including the right to enter into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(6) the thing is a use of interests in shares` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the exercise of any rights, or of any control or influence, arising from the interests (including the right to enter into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (4)(b) to the use of interests in shares is to the exercise of any rights or of any control or influence arising from those interests"

-- s 988(7): "agreement" includes any agreement or arrangement; references to provisions of an agreement include undertakings, expectations or understandings operative under an arrangement, and any provision express or implied, absolute or not.
-- src:13839 | (a) “agreement” includes any agreement or arrangement;
@ref s 988(7)(a) Associates (src:13839-13839)
GIVEN `the thing is an agreement or an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(7)(a) the thing is an agreement` MEANS
    IF `the thing is an agreement or an arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“agreement” includes any agreement or arrangement"

-- src:13840 | (b) references to provisions of an agreement include—
-- src:13841 | (i) undertakings, expectations or understandings operative under an arrangement, and
-- src:13842 | (ii) any provision whether express or implied and whether absolute or not.
@ref s 988(7)(b) Associates (src:13840-13842)
GIVEN `the thing is an undertaking, expectation or understanding operative under an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a provision of the agreement, express or implied, absolute or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(7)(b) the thing is a provision of an agreement` MEANS
    IF `the thing is an undertaking, expectation or understanding operative under an arrangement` OR `the thing is a provision of the agreement, express or implied, absolute or not`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to provisions of an agreement include"

-- s 988(1): "associate", in relation to an offeror, means a nominee, a group company or its nominee, a body corporate he is substantially interested in, a party to a share acquisition agreement, or (for an individual) his spouse, civil partner and minor children and step-children.
-- src:13819 | (1) In this Chapter “associate”, in relation to an offeror, means—
-- src:13820 | (a) a nominee of the offeror,
-- src:13821 | (b) a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror or a nominee of such a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary,
-- src:13822 | (c) a body corporate in which the offeror is substantially interested,
-- src:13823 | (d) a person who is, or is a nominee of, a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror, or
-- src:13824 | (e) (where the offeror is an individual) his spouse or civil partner and any minor child or step-child of his.
@ref s 988(1) Associates (src:13819-13824)
GIVEN `the person is a nominee of the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988(1)(b) the person is a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a nominee of such a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988(3) the offeror is substantially interested in the person as a body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 988(4) the person is, or is a nominee of, a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offeror is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the offeror's spouse or civil partner, or his minor child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 988(1) the person is an associate of the offeror` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a nominee of the offeror`
         OR  `s 988(1)(b) the person is a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  `the person is a nominee of such a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary`
         OR  `s 988(3) the offeror is substantially interested in the person as a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  `s 988(4) the person is, or is a nominee of, a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  (`the offeror is an individual` AND `the person is the offeror's spouse or civil partner, or his minor child or step-child`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       `s 988(1)(b) the person is a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror` EQUALS NOTHING
              OR  `s 988(3) the offeror is substantially interested in the person as a body corporate` EQUALS NOTHING
              OR  `s 988(4) the person is, or is a nominee of, a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on section 1159 or on section 988(3) or (4), whose answer is not known
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Chapter “associate”, in relation to an offeror, means—"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Takeover offers (ss 974 to 978)`

-- s 975(2) and (3): shares subject to a contract intended to secure acceptance are not "already held by the offeror" (in Scotland, "by deed and" is omitted).
DECLARE `s 975(3) part of the United Kingdom` IS ONE OF
    `s 975(3) Scotland`
    `s 975(3) England and Wales or Northern Ireland`

-- src:13568 | (2) The reference in section 974(2) to shares already held by the offeror does not include a reference to shares that are the subject of a contract—
-- src:13569 | (a) intended to secure that the holder of the shares will accept the offer when it is made, and
-- src:13570 | (b) entered into—
-- src:13571 | (i) by deed and for no consideration,
-- src:13572 | (ii) for consideration of negligible value, or
-- src:13573 | (iii) for consideration consisting of a promise by the offeror to make the offer.
-- src:13574 | (3) In relation to Scotland, this section applies as if the words “by deed and” in subsection (2)(b)(i) were omitted.
@ref s 975(2)-(3) Shares already held by the offeror etc (src:13568-13574)
GIVEN `the contract is intended to secure that the holder of the shares will accept the offer when it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into by deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into for no consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into for consideration of negligible value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into for consideration consisting of a promise by the offeror to make the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      part IS A `s 975(3) part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 975(2) the contract is one whose shares are not shares already held by the offeror` MEANS
    IF `the contract is intended to secure that the holder of the shares will accept the offer when it is made`
       AND (`paragraph (b)(i) is satisfied` OR `the contract was entered into for consideration of negligible value` OR `the contract was entered into for consideration consisting of a promise by the offeror to make the offer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is of "shares that are the subject of a contract— (a) intended to secure that the holder of the shares will accept the offer when it is made, and (b) entered into" in one of the three ways
    WHERE
        -- (b)(i) is "by deed and for no consideration"; for Scotland, subsection (3) omits "by deed and"
        `paragraph (b)(i) is satisfied` MEANS
            CONSIDER part
            WHEN `s 975(3) Scotland` THEN `the contract was entered into for no consideration`
            WHEN `s 975(3) England and Wales or Northern Ireland` THEN `the contract was entered into by deed` AND `the contract was entered into for no consideration`

-- s 975(1): "shares already held by the offeror" includes shares he has contracted to acquire, unconditionally or subject to conditions, but see (2).
-- src:13566 | (1) The reference in section 974(2) to shares already held by the offeror includes a reference to shares that he has contracted to acquire, whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met.
-- src:13567 | This is subject to subsection (2).
@ref s 975(1) Shares already held by the offeror etc (src:13566-13567)
GIVEN `the offeror holds the shares at the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has contracted unconditionally to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has contracted to acquire the shares subject to conditions being met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 975(2) the contract is one whose shares are not shares already held by the offeror` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 975(1) the shares are shares already held by the offeror` MEANS
    IF `s 975(2) the contract is one whose shares are not shares already held by the offeror` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include a reference to shares that are the subject of a contract"
    ELSE IF `the offeror holds the shares at the date of the offer` OR `the offeror has contracted unconditionally to acquire the shares` OR `the offeror has contracted to acquire the shares subject to conditions being met`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The reference in section 974(2) to shares already held by the offeror includes a reference to shares that he has contracted to acquire, whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met."

-- s 975(4): the condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied where the offer does not extend to shares associates hold or have contracted to acquire, and would be satisfied if it did.
-- src:13575 | (4) The condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied where—
-- src:13576 | (a) the offer does not extend to shares that associates of the offeror hold or have contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met), and
-- src:13577 | (b) the condition would be satisfied if the offer did extend to those shares.
-- src:13578 | (For further provision about such shares, see section 977(2)).
@ref s 975(4) Shares already held by the offeror etc (src:13575-13578)
GIVEN `the offer does not extend to shares that associates of the offeror hold or have contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in section 974(2) would be satisfied if the offer did extend to those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 975(4) the condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the offer does not extend to shares that associates of the offeror hold or have contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)` AND `the condition in section 974(2) would be satisfied if the offer did extend to those shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied where— (a) the offer does not extend to shares that associates of the offeror hold or have contracted to acquire"

-- s 974(2): the first condition: an offer to acquire all the shares, or all the shares of one or more classes, other than those the offeror already holds.
-- src:13543 | (2) The first condition is that it is an offer to acquire—
-- src:13544 | (a) all the shares in a company, or
-- src:13545 | (b) where there is more than one class of shares in a company, all the shares of one or more classes,
-- src:13546 | other than shares that at the date of the offer are already held by the offeror.
-- src:13547 | Section 975 contains provision supplementing this subsection.
@ref s 974(2) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13543-13547)
GIVEN `the offer is to acquire all the shares in the company, other than shares already held by the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is more than one class of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes, other than shares already held by the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 975(4) the condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(2) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 975(4) the condition in section 974(2) is treated as satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the offer is to acquire all the shares in the company, other than shares already held by the offeror` OR (`there is more than one class of shares in the company` AND `the offer is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes, other than shares already held by the offeror`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that it is an offer to acquire— (a) all the shares in a company, or (b) where there is more than one class of shares in a company, all the shares of one or more classes"

-- s 976(2): the dividend case: a difference in consideration that merely reflects a difference in dividend entitlement.
-- src:13581 | (2) This subsection applies where—
-- src:13582 | (a) shares carry an entitlement to a particular dividend which other shares of the same class, by reason of being allotted later, do not carry,
-- src:13583 | (b) there is a difference in the value of consideration offered for the shares allotted earlier as against that offered for those allotted later,
-- src:13584 | (c) that difference merely reflects the difference in entitlement to the dividend, and
-- src:13585 | (d) the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for that difference.
@ref s 976(2) Cases where offer treated as being on same terms (src:13581-13585)
GIVEN `shares carry an entitlement to a particular dividend which other shares of the same class, by reason of being allotted later, do not carry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a difference in the value of consideration offered for the shares allotted earlier as against those allotted later` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that difference merely reflects the difference in entitlement to the dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for that difference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 976(2) the subsection applies` MEANS
    IF       `shares carry an entitlement to a particular dividend which other shares of the same class, by reason of being allotted later, do not carry`
         AND `there is a difference in the value of consideration offered for the shares allotted earlier as against those allotted later`
         AND `that difference merely reflects the difference in entitlement to the dividend`
         AND `the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for that difference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies where— (a) shares carry an entitlement to a particular dividend which other shares of the same class, by reason of being allotted later, do not carry"

-- s 976(3): the foreign-law case: the law outside the United Kingdom precludes consideration in the specified form, and equivalent value in another form is available.
-- src:13586 | (3) This subsection applies where—
-- src:13587 | (a) the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:13588 | (i) precludes an offer of consideration in the form, or any of the forms, specified in the terms of the offer (“the specified form”), or
-- src:13589 | (ii) precludes it except after compliance by the offeror with conditions with which he is unable to comply or which he regards as unduly onerous,
-- src:13590 | (b) the persons to whom an offer of consideration in the specified form is precluded are able to receive consideration in another form that is of substantially equivalent value, and
-- src:13591 | (c) the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for the fact that an offer of consideration in the specified form to those persons is precluded.
@ref s 976(3) Cases where offer treated as being on same terms (src:13586-13591)
GIVEN `the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom precludes an offer of consideration in the form, or any of the forms, specified in the terms of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that law precludes it except after compliance by the offeror with conditions with which he is unable to comply or which he regards as unduly onerous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons to whom an offer of consideration in the specified form is precluded are able to receive consideration in another form that is of substantially equivalent value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for the fact that an offer of consideration in the specified form to those persons is precluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 976(3) the subsection applies` MEANS
    IF       (`the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom precludes an offer of consideration in the form, or any of the forms, specified in the terms of the offer` OR `that law precludes it except after compliance by the offeror with conditions with which he is unable to comply or which he regards as unduly onerous`)
         AND `the persons to whom an offer of consideration in the specified form is precluded are able to receive consideration in another form that is of substantially equivalent value`
         AND `the condition in section 974(3) would be satisfied but for the fact that an offer of consideration in the specified form to those persons is precluded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies where— (a) the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom—"

-- s 976(1): the condition in section 974(3) is treated as satisfied where subsection (2) or (3) applies.
-- src:13580 | (1) The condition in section 974(3) (terms of offer to be the same for all shares or all shares of particular classes) is treated as satisfied where subsection (2) or (3) below applies.
@ref s 976(1) Cases where offer treated as being on same terms (src:13580-13580)
GIVEN `s 976(2) the subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 976(3) the subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 976(1) the condition in section 974(3) is treated as satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 976(2) the subsection applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 976(3) the subsection applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition in section 974(3) (terms of offer to be the same for all shares or all shares of particular classes) is treated as satisfied where subsection (2) or (3) below applies."

-- s 974(3): the second condition: the terms of the offer are the same for all the shares, or for all the shares of each class.
-- src:13548 | (3) The second condition is that the terms of the offer are the same—
-- src:13549 | (a) in relation to all the shares to which the offer relates, or
-- src:13550 | (b) where the shares to which the offer relates include shares of different classes, in relation to all the shares of each class.
-- src:13551 | Section 976 contains provision treating this condition as satisfied in certain circumstances.
@ref s 974(3) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13548-13551)
GIVEN `the terms of the offer are the same in relation to all the shares to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares to which the offer relates include shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the offer are the same in relation to all the shares of each class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 976(1) the condition in section 974(3) is treated as satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(3) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 976(1) the condition in section 974(3) is treated as satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the terms of the offer are the same in relation to all the shares to which the offer relates` OR (`the shares to which the offer relates include shares of different classes` AND `the terms of the offer are the same in relation to all the shares of each class`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that the terms of the offer are the same— (a) in relation to all the shares to which the offer relates"

-- s 974(1): an offer to acquire shares in a company is a takeover offer if the two conditions are satisfied.
-- src:13542 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter an offer to acquire shares in a company is a “takeover offer” if the following two conditions are satisfied in relation to the offer.
@ref s 974(1) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13542-13542)
GIVEN `s 974(2) the first condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 974(3) the second condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(1) the offer is a takeover offer` MEANS
    IF `s 974(2) the first condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 974(3) the second condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offer to acquire shares in a company is a “takeover offer” if the following two conditions are satisfied in relation to the offer"
    ELSE IF `s 974(2) the first condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 974(3) the second condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- s 974(6): "relevant treasury shares" and "specified date".
