    IF `the date is specified in, or determined in accordance with, the terms of the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified date” means a date specified in or determined in accordance with the terms of the offer"

-- s 974(4): "shares" means shares, other than relevant treasury shares, that have been allotted on the date of the offer.
-- src:13552 | (4) In subsections (1) to (3) “shares” means shares, other than relevant treasury shares, that have been allotted on the date of the offer (but see subsection (5)).
@ref s 974(4) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13552-13552)
