      `s 974(6) the shares are relevant treasury shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(4) the shares are shares for subsections (1) to (3)` MEANS
    IF `the shares have been allotted on the date of the offer` AND `s 974(6) the shares are relevant treasury shares` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In subsections (1) to (3) “shares” means shares, other than relevant treasury shares, that have been allotted on the date of the offer"

-- s 974(5): a takeover offer may include later-allotted shares and relevant treasury shares.
-- src:13553 | (5) A takeover offer may include among the shares to which it relates—
-- src:13554 | (a) all or any shares that are allotted after the date of the offer but before a specified date;
-- src:13555 | (b) all or any relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury shares before a specified date;
-- src:13556 | (c) all or any other relevant treasury shares.
@ref s 974(5) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13553-13556)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted after the date of the offer but before a specified date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury shares before a specified date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are other relevant treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(5) the shares may be included among the shares to which the offer relates` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted after the date of the offer but before a specified date` OR `the shares are relevant treasury shares that cease to be held as treasury shares before a specified date` OR `the shares are other relevant treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A takeover offer may include among the shares to which it relates" the three kinds listed

-- s 974(7): a revision of the terms under a revision provision is not a fresh offer, and the date of the offer stays the date of the original offer.
-- src:13562 | (7) Where the terms of an offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms, then, if the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision—
-- src:13563 | (a) the revision is not to be regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as the making of a fresh offer, and
-- src:13564 | (b) references in this Chapter to the date of the offer are accordingly to be read as references to the date of the original offer.
@ref s 974(7) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13562-13564)
GIVEN `the terms of the offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 974(7)(a) the revision is regarded as the making of a fresh offer` MEANS
    IF `the terms of the offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms` AND `the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the revision is not to be regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as the making of a fresh offer"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for terms that make such provision, "if the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision"

-- src:13562 | (7) Where the terms of an offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms, then, if the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision—
-- src:13563 | (a) the revision is not to be regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as the making of a fresh offer, and
-- src:13564 | (b) references in this Chapter to the date of the offer are accordingly to be read as references to the date of the original offer.
@ref s 974(7) Meaning of “takeover offer” (src:13562-13564)
GIVEN `the terms of the offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the original offer` IS A DATE
      `s 991(1) the date of the offer on the revised footing` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 974(7)(b) the date of the offer` MEANS
    IF `the terms of the offer make provision for their revision and for acceptances on the previous terms to be treated as acceptances on the revised terms` AND `the terms of the offer are revised in accordance with that provision`
    THEN JUST `the date of the original offer`
    ELSE `s 991(1) the date of the offer on the revised footing`

-- s 977(1): shares the offeror acquires, or unconditionally contracts to acquire, during the offer otherwise than by acceptances are treated as excluded from those to which the offer relates.
-- src:13593 | (1) Where a takeover offer is made and, during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror—
-- src:13594 | (a) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but
-- src:13595 | (b) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer,
-- src:13596 | those shares are treated for the purposes of this Chapter as excluded from those to which the offer relates.
@ref s 977(1) Shares to which an offer relates (src:13593-13596)
GIVEN `the date of the offer` IS A DATE
      `the day the offer can no longer be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire the shares to which the offer relates` IS A DATE
      `the offeror does so by virtue of acceptances of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 977(1) the shares are treated as excluded from those to which the offer relates` MEANS
    IF `the day the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire the shares to which the offer relates` AT LEAST `the date of the offer` AND `the day the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire the shares to which the offer relates` AT MOST `the day the offer can no longer be accepted` AND NOT (`the offeror does so by virtue of acceptances of the offer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a takeover offer is made and, during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror— (a) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but (b) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer"

-- s 977(2): shares an associate of the offeror holds or has contracted to acquire are not treated as shares to which the offer relates.
-- src:13597 | (2) For the purposes of this Chapter shares that an associate of the offeror holds or has contracted to acquire, whether at the date of the offer or subsequently, are not treated as shares to which the offer relates, even if the offer extends to such shares.
-- src:13598 | In this subsection “contracted” means contracted unconditionally or subject to conditions being met.
@ref s 977(2) Shares to which an offer relates (src:13597-13598)
GIVEN `an associate of the offeror holds the shares at the date of the offer or subsequently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an associate of the offeror has contracted unconditionally to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an associate of the offeror has contracted to acquire the shares subject to conditions being met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 977(2) the shares are treated as shares to which the offer relates` MEANS
    IF `an associate of the offeror holds the shares at the date of the offer or subsequently` OR `an associate of the offeror has contracted unconditionally to acquire the shares` OR `an associate of the offeror has contracted to acquire the shares subject to conditions being met`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares that an associate of the offeror holds or has contracted to acquire, whether at the date of the offer or subsequently, are not treated as shares to which the offer relates, even if the offer extends to such shares"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says which shares are not treated as shares to which the offer relates, not which are

-- s 977(3): this section is subject to section 979(8) and (9).
-- src:13599 | (3) This section is subject to section 979(8) and (9).
@ref s 977(3) Shares to which an offer relates (src:13599-13599)
GIVEN `the purposes are those of section 979` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 979(10) applies to the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 977(3) the exclusion applies for the purposes` MEANS
    IF `the purposes are those of section 979` AND `section 979(10) applies to the acquisition`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section is subject to section 979(8) and (9)", which say the shares are not excluded for the purposes of section 979 when subsection (10) applies
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 978(1): the offer is not prevented from being a takeover offer by non-communication to shareholders abroad, if the conditions hold.
-- src:13601 | (1) Where there are holders of shares in a company to whom an offer to acquire shares in the company is not communicated, that does not prevent the offer from being a takeover offer for the purposes of this Chapter if—
-- src:13602 | (a) those shareholders have no registered address in the United Kingdom,
-- src:13603 | (b) the offer was not communicated to those shareholders in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:13604 | (c) either—
-- src:13605 | (i) the offer is published in the Gazette, or
-- src:13606 | (ii) the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in the United Kingdom or on a website, and a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website.
@ref s 978(1) Effect of impossibility etc of communicating or accepting offer (src:13601-13606)
GIVEN `there are holders of shares to whom the offer is not communicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shareholders have no registered address in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer was not communicated to them in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in the United Kingdom or on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 978(1) the offer is not prevented from being a takeover offer by its not being communicated` MEANS
    IF       `there are holders of shares to whom the offer is not communicated`
         AND `those shareholders have no registered address in the United Kingdom`
         AND `the offer was not communicated to them in order not to contravene the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
         AND (`the offer is published in the Gazette` OR (`the offer can be inspected, or a copy of it obtained, at a place in the United Kingdom or on a website` AND `a notice is published in the Gazette specifying the address of that place or website`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that does not prevent the offer from being a takeover offer for the purposes of this Chapter if— (a) those shareholders have no registered address in the United Kingdom"

-- s 978(2): impossibility or difficulty of accepting, by reason of foreign law, does not prevent the offer from being a takeover offer.
-- src:13607 | (2) Where an offer is made to acquire shares in a company and there are persons for whom, by reason of the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom, it is impossible to accept the offer, or more difficult to do so, that does not prevent the offer from being a takeover offer for the purposes of this Chapter.
