`s 978(3)(a) it may be inferred that the offer cannot be a takeover offer unless the requirements of subsection (1)(a) to (c) are met` MEANS
    IF `the offer is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not to be inferred— (a) that an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company cannot be a takeover offer for the purposes of this Chapter unless the requirements of paragraphs (a) to (c) of subsection (1) are met"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "an offer which is not communicated to every holder of shares in the company"

-- src:13610 | (b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept cannot be a takeover offer for those purposes unless the reason for the impossibility or difficulty is the one mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 978(3)(b) Effect of impossibility etc of communicating or accepting offer (src:13610-13610)
GIVEN `the offer is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 978(3)(b) it may be inferred that the offer cannot be a takeover offer unless the reason is the one mentioned in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the offer is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) that an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept cannot be a takeover offer for those purposes unless the reason for the impossibility or difficulty is the one mentioned in subsection (2)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "an offer which is impossible, or more difficult, for certain persons to accept"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Joint offers (s 987)`

-- s 987(2) and (3): the conditions for the rights in sections 979 and 983 are satisfied by joint offerors acquiring jointly (for acceptances) or jointly or separately (otherwise).
DECLARE `s 987 kind of acquisition` IS ONE OF
    `s 987(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer`
    `s 987(2)(b) in another way`

-- src:13802 | (2) The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 979 are satisfied—
-- src:13803 | (a) in the case of acquisitions by virtue of acceptances of the offer, by the joint offerors acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly;
-- src:13804 | (b) in other cases, by the joint offerors acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately.
@ref s 987(2) Joint offers (src:13802-13804)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 987 kind of acquisition`
      `the joint offerors acquire or unconditionally contract to acquire the necessary shares jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the joint offerors acquire or unconditionally contract to acquire the necessary shares separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(2) the conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 979 are satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 987(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer` THEN
        IF `the joint offerors acquire or unconditionally contract to acquire the necessary shares jointly`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): for acquisitions by virtue of acceptances the conditions are satisfied "by the joint offerors acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly"
    WHEN `s 987(2)(b) in another way` THEN
        IF `the joint offerors acquire or unconditionally contract to acquire the necessary shares jointly` OR `the joint offerors acquire or unconditionally contract to acquire the necessary shares separately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): in other cases the conditions are satisfied by acquiring "either jointly or separately"

-- src:13805 | (3) The conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 983 are satisfied—
-- src:13806 | (a) in the case of acquisitions by virtue of acceptances of the offer, by the joint offerors acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly;
-- src:13807 | (b) in other cases, by the joint offerors acquiring or contracting (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met) to acquire the necessary shares either jointly or separately.
@ref s 987(3) Joint offers (src:13805-13807)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 987 kind of acquisition`
      `the joint offerors acquire or contract (unconditionally or subject to conditions) to acquire the necessary shares jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the joint offerors acquire or contract (unconditionally or subject to conditions) to acquire the necessary shares separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(3) the conditions for the exercise of the rights conferred by section 983 are satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 987(2)(a) by virtue of acceptances of the offer` THEN
        IF `the joint offerors acquire or contract (unconditionally or subject to conditions) to acquire the necessary shares jointly`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): for acquisitions by virtue of acceptances the conditions are satisfied "by the joint offerors acquiring or unconditionally contracting to acquire the necessary shares jointly"
    WHEN `s 987(2)(b) in another way` THEN
        IF `the joint offerors acquire or contract (unconditionally or subject to conditions) to acquire the necessary shares jointly` OR `the joint offerors acquire or contract (unconditionally or subject to conditions) to acquire the necessary shares separately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): in other cases the conditions are satisfied by acquiring or contracting "either jointly or separately"

-- s 987(4): the offeror's rights under sections 979 to 985 are joint rights and its obligations joint and several obligations of the joint offerors.
DECLARE `s 987(4) position of the offeror` IS ONE OF
    `s 987(4) a right of the offeror`
    `s 987(4) an obligation of the offeror`

DECLARE `s 987(4) how the joint offerors hold it` IS ONE OF
    `s 987(4) a joint right`
    `s 987(4) a joint and several obligation`

-- src:13808 | (4) Subject to the following provisions, the rights and obligations of the offeror under sections 979 to 985 are respectively joint rights and joint and several obligations of the joint offerors.
@ref s 987(4) Joint offers (src:13808-13808)
GIVEN position IS A `s 987(4) position of the offeror`
GIVETH A `s 987(4) how the joint offerors hold it`
`s 987(4) how the joint offerors hold the position` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 987(4) a right of the offeror` THEN `s 987(4) a joint right`
    WHEN `s 987(4) an obligation of the offeror` THEN `s 987(4) a joint and several obligation`

-- s 987(5): a notice or document is complied with if given or sent by or to any of the joint offerors (but see (6)).
-- src:13809 | (5) A provision of sections 979 to 986 that requires or authorises a notice or other document to be given or sent by or to the joint offerors is complied with if the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of them (but see subsection (6)).
@ref s 987(5) Joint offers (src:13809-13809)
GIVEN `the notice or document is required or authorised by sections 979 to 986 to be given or sent by or to the joint offerors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or sent by or to any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the statutory declaration required by section 980(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(5) the notice or document requirement is complied with` MEANS
    IF `it is the statutory declaration required by section 980(4)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(but see subsection (6))": the statutory declaration is governed by subsection (6)
    ELSE IF `the notice or document is required or authorised by sections 979 to 986 to be given or sent by or to the joint offerors` AND `it is given or sent by or to any of them`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement "is complied with if the notice or document is given or sent by or to any of them"

-- s 987(6): the statutory declaration must be made by all the joint offerors and, where one is a company, signed by a director of it.
-- src:13810 | (6) The statutory declaration required by section 980(4) must be made by all of the joint offerors and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of that company.
@ref s 987(6) Joint offers (src:13810-13810)
GIVEN `the declaration is made by all of the joint offerors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each joint offeror that is a company has its part signed by a director of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(6) the statutory declaration meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is made by all of the joint offerors` AND `each joint offeror that is a company has its part signed by a director of that company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statutory declaration required by section 980(4) must be made by all of the joint offerors and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of that company."

-- s 987(7) and (8): where the references to the offeror are read as the joint offerors (or any of them, or such of them as they may determine).
DECLARE `s 987(7) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 987(7) section 974`
    `s 987(7) section 975`
    `s 987(7) section 976`
    `s 987(7) section 977`
    `s 987(7) section 979(9)`
    `s 987(7) section 981(6)`
    `s 987(7) section 983(8)`
    `s 987(7) section 988`
    `s 987(8) section 981(7)`
    `s 987(8) section 981(8)`
    `s 987 another provision`

DECLARE `s 987 how the offeror is read` IS ONE OF
    `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    `s 987(8) the joint offerors or such of them as they may determine`
    `s 987 not covered`

-- src:13811 | (7) In sections 974 to 977, 979(9), 981(6), 983(8) and 988 references to the offeror are to be read as references to the joint offerors or any of them.
-- src:13812 | (8) In section 981(7) and (8) references to the offeror are to be read as references to the joint offerors or such of them as they may determine.
@ref s 987(7)-(8) Joint offers (src:13811-13812)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 987(7) provision`
GIVETH A `s 987 how the offeror is read`
`s 987(7)-(8) how a reference to the offeror in the provision is read` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 974` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 975` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 976` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 977` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 979(9)` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 981(6)` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 983(8)` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(7) section 988` THEN `s 987(7) the joint offerors or any of them`
    WHEN `s 987(8) section 981(7)` THEN `s 987(8) the joint offerors or such of them as they may determine`
    WHEN `s 987(8) section 981(8)` THEN `s 987(8) the joint offerors or such of them as they may determine`
    WHEN `s 987 another provision` THEN `s 987 not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsections name these provisions only

-- s 987(9): references to the offeror being no longer able to provide the consideration are read as none of the joint offerors being able to.
-- src:13813 | (9) In sections 981(5)(a) and 985(5)(a) references to the offeror being no longer able to provide the relevant consideration are to be read as references to none of the joint offerors being able to do so.
@ref s 987(9) Joint offers (src:13813-13813)
GIVEN `none of the joint offerors is able to provide the relevant consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(9) the offeror is no longer able to provide the relevant consideration` MEANS
    IF `none of the joint offerors is able to provide the relevant consideration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to the offeror being no longer able to provide the relevant consideration are to be read as references to none of the joint offerors being able to do so"

-- s 987(10): in section 986 references to the offeror are to the joint offerors, except that an application under (3) or (9) may be made by any of them and the tracing reference is to none of them having been able to trace.
-- src:13815 | (a) an application under subsection (3) or (9) may be made by any of them, and
@ref s 987(10)(a) Joint offers (src:13815-13815)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (3) or (9) of section 986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by one of the joint offerors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(10)(a) the application may be made by the joint offeror` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection (3) or (9) of section 986` AND `it is made by one of the joint offerors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is "an application under subsection (3) or (9) may be made by any of them"

-- src:13816 | (b) the reference in subsection (9)(a) to the offeror having been unable to trace one or more of the persons holding shares is to be read as a reference to none of the offerors having been able to do so.
@ref s 987(10)(b) Joint offers (src:13816-13816)
GIVEN `none of the joint offerors has been able to trace the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 987(10)(b) the offeror has been unable to trace the person` MEANS
    IF `none of the joint offerors has been able to trace the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference in subsection (9)(a) to the offeror having been unable to trace one or more of the persons holding shares is to be read as a reference to none of the offerors having been able to do so"
